        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Patrickbot",
          "email": "patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us",
          "date": "2026-11-06 00:47:31.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-17637 tests: use non-zero data in sanity 56xk",
        "message": "LU-17637 tests: use non-zero data in sanity 56xk\n\nsanity test_56xk times 'lfs mirror resync -W 1M' on a 5MB file\nand fails with \"too fast (0 < 0.95 * 5)\" on ZFS. The file is\nwritten from /dev/zero, which ZFS compression stores as holes.\nResync skips holes (SEEK_DATA), so nothing is copied and the\nbandwidth limit never applies.\n\nWrite the file from /dev/urandom so there is data to copy.\nWith lz4 compression enabled on the ZFS OSTs, the test failed\n\"too fast\" before this change and passes with it.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial fstype=zfs testlist=sanity env=ONLY=56xk\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I66d828d9cf23e7527cbf5e08439105d7181d0d26\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
